cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the IGLA trainer pipeline in research, please cite it as below."
title: "trios-trainer-igla - IGLA Training Pipeline (Trinity S3AI)"
abstract: "trios-trainer-igla is a from-scratch Rust byte-level trainer (no PyTorch) together with the reproducibility-grading method it exists to demonstrate: checkpoints are written atomically and hashed, every run emits a JSON sidecar recording the corpus hashes, the eval grid, the toolchain, the binary hash and the platform, and a result is quoted only with the conditions under which it holds. Same-machine determinism is demonstrated (identical parameters yield byte-identical checkpoints); byte-identity ACROSS CPU architectures is not claimed and is measured to fail, so the platform is declared rather than assumed. The repository is also the ONE-SOURCE-OF-TRUTH training pipeline for the IGLA architecture-search race of the Trinity S3AI / GOLDEN SUNFLOWERS research programme, and owns the 5-lane migration L-T1..L-T5, the embargo ledger and the triplet format. It makes no capability claim: the calibration fixture is a ~196.6K-parameter byte model, and withdrawn numbers are listed in docs/audit/HONEST_FINDINGS.md. Anchor: phi^2 + phi^-2 = 3. Canonical Zenodo community: https://zenodo.org/communities/trinity-s3ai/."
authors:
